## Policy Evaluation Logic

| Request | IAM policy | Bucket policy | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| `internal/roster.txt` | Allow (Resource: *) | Allow (internal/*) | **ALLOWED** |
| `confidential/record.txt` | Allow (Resource: *) | Explicit **Deny** (confidential/*) | **DENIED** |

### Simple explanation

> - An **identity-based policy** is attached to the IAM user - it says what *that user* can do.
> - A **resource-based policy** is attached to the bucket - it says which *principals* may access it.
>
> An explicit `Deny` in either policy **always overrides any `Allow`**. The bucket policy Deny on `confidential/*` is stronger than the analyst's broad IAM Allow.

