# 10. Task 7 - Versioning, Delete Markers and Data Remanence

## Objective

Demonstrate that deleting an S3 object **does not remove previous versions** when versioning is enabled. Old data can survive deletion - this is called **data remanence**.

## Steps

```bash
# Enable versioning
aws $EP s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket $BUCKET \
  --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled
aws $EP s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket $BUCKET
# Create version 2 (with real diagnosis)
echo 'Patient: Ahmad bin Ali, Diagnosis: hypertension' > rec-v2.txt
aws $EP s3api put-object --bucket $BUCKET --key confidential/record.txt \
  --body rec-v2.txt --query VersionId --output text
# Create version 3 (redacted)
echo 'Patient: [REDACTED], Diagnosis: [REDACTED]' > rec-v3.txt
aws $EP s3api put-object --bucket $BUCKET --key confidential/record.txt \
  --body rec-v3.txt --query VersionId --output text
# List all versions
aws $EP s3api list-object-versions --bucket $BUCKET \
  --prefix confidential/record.txt \
  --query 'Versions[].[VersionId,IsLatest,Size]' --output table
# Delete the object normally
aws $EP s3api delete-object --bucket $BUCKET --key confidential/record.txt
# Verify delete marker was created
aws $EP s3api list-object-versions --bucket $BUCKET \
  --prefix confidential/record.txt \
  --query 'DeleteMarkers[].[VersionId,IsLatest]' --output table
# Recover the original version
aws $EP s3api get-object --bucket $BUCKET \
  --key confidential/record.txt --version-id null recovered.txt
cat recovered.txt
```

### Evidence

![Evidence Image 24 - Versioning enabled on the bucket](lab6_evidence_images/image24.png)

**What the screenshot shows:** `put-bucket-versioning` with `Status=Enabled` succeeded. `get-bucket-versioning` returned `"Status": "Enabled"`.

![Evidence Image 25 - Version 2 and Version 3 created for confidential record](lab6_evidence_images/image25.png)

**What the screenshot shows:** Version 2 (hypertension diagnosis) returned VersionId `AaCRD.Rm774tUhITK9V60RozrnfGTgZr`. Version 3 (redacted) returned VersionId `AaCRD.RmNH7ZS4sGI3JTg360yuGEQ0ImIe`.

![Evidence Image 26 - All three versions visible in the version list](lab6_evidence_images/image26.png)

**What the screenshot shows:** The version table shows three versions: `AaCRD.RmNH7ZS4sGI3JTg360yuGEQ0ImIe` (IsLatest: True, 43 bytes), `AaCRD.Rm774tUhITK9V60RozrnfGTgZr` (IsLatest: False, 48 bytes), `null` (IsLatest: False, 48 bytes).

![Evidence Image 27 - Delete marker created, old versions remain underneath](lab6_evidence_images/image27.png)

**What the screenshot shows:** `delete-object` returned `"DeleteMarker": true` with a new VersionId. `list-object-versions` shows the delete marker (`AaCRD.Ro3JfG8N8e_iKp5CPONXFpOhia`, `IsLatest: True`) - but the data is NOT destroyed.

![Evidence Image 28 - Original confidential record recovered after deletion](lab6_evidence_images/image28.png)

**What the screenshot shows:** `get-object --version-id null` succeeded (ContentLength: 48). `cat recovered.txt` printed: **"Patient: Ahmad bin Ali, Diagnosis: confidential"** - the original data was fully recoverable after deletion.

### Simple explanation

> With versioning enabled, `delete-object` does:
> ```
> Creates a delete marker on top
>     -> All old versions remain underneath, still recoverable
> ```
>
> `delete-object` alone is **not sufficient** for a right-to-erasure request. All versions must be explicitly deleted by Version ID, or the encryption key must be destroyed (cryptographic erasure in Task 8).

